Section 2: Governance Structure (RACI)

Who is involved in governing the platform? - Box AI governance involves Box's leadership team and multiple internal departments working within a structured framework. The platform is controlled by Box's built-in permissions system, which ensures customers retain authority over their data and can determine who accesses AI features and content.

Role                                                                     Responsibility

Operating Committee (OpCo)                                               Sets overall AI strategy, priorities, best practices, and usage guidelines
Legal, Security, Compliance, Product, Engineering, Supplier Management   Reviews compliance, security, and industry standards alignment
Functional Leaders (Sales, Marketing, Engineering, Customer Support)     Applies OpCo guidelines to departmental AI strategy and processes
AI Managers                                                              Oversees individual AI agents, monitors performance, and ensures compliance
Box Administrators & End Users                                           Enable/disable Box AI features and determine content applicability

